course: dictionary
lesson: 3621
title: Final: last, or cannot be changed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Final is an adjective, and most often it means last, coming at the end. «The final score» is the score after every point has been counted. Look at the words around it to find the meaning.
explain: A final can also be a noun: the last game or race that decides the winner. «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» Dev wins the last game of the tournament. Finals can also be the last tests of a school year or course.
explain: Final can mean that something cannot be changed. «The referee's word is final» means the referee has decided, and arguing will not change it. The clue is in the sentence: the referee has made a decision that stands. Swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
fact: Final means last, coming at the end.
fact: A final is the last game or race that decides the winner.
fact: Finals are the last exams of a school year or course.
fact: Final can mean that cannot be changed, as in «my answer is final».
fact: Other words in the same family include finally, meaning at last, and finish, meaning to end.
exercise: «The final chapter of the book was the most exciting.» What does final mean here? | *Last, at the end | Very short | First of all | Happy
exercise: Dev beats Sam in the chess final. What is the final? | A game played at lunch | A quick practice game | *The last game that decides the winner | The first move of the game
exercise: «The referee's word is final.» What does final mean here? | It is said quietly | It is the last word of the match | *It cannot be changed | It is written in ink
test: «My answer is final.» What does final mean? | *It cannot be changed | It is the first answer | It is wrong | It is written in pencil
test: The school finals are held in June. What are finals? | Lessons with a friend | The first tests of the year | *The last exams of a school year or course | Games in the playground
exam: In «the final step of the sum gives the answer», what does final mean? | Earliest | Easiest | *Last | Loudest
